{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2184","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2184","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2184\",\"parent_revision\":\"ccc86aeb5581d81b34d0af68e2f1bb3216fdf24e\",\"root_revision\":\"0784ddf3073b92c97d18c8670a65b4d5f8049406e888dba8414d8e99faab2fe8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **dh doctor diagnostic command for plugin health, hook wiring, and stale residue detection** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md \u2014 pattern: harness doctor and harness doctor --residue commands diagnose hook installation, binary presence, and detect leftover references to deleted code from previous versions\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-08)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\\\n\\\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\\\n|-------|--------|--------|\\\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description: 5 named checks, `OK|WARN|FAIL` output per check |\\\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Explicitly listed: hook wiring, MCP reachability, state dir hygiene, cache freshness, residue detection (`--residue` flag) |\\\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | `hooks.json`, hook `.cjs` scripts, MCP tools (`backlog_view`, `sam_plan`), `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/`, source and cache `plugin.json` |\\\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | Exit codes 0/1/2, 30s MCP timeout, 24h orphan file threshold, PEP 723 inline script format (`uv run --script`) |\\\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | 7 hooks confirmed in hooks.json; 16 existing scripts with PEP 723 headers in `scripts/`; state dir layout documented in CLAUDE.md |\\\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Measurable signal section gives exact expected stdout for the passing case and the broken-link case |\\\\n\\\\nNo missing inputs. No blocker questions for the human. Item is ready for planning.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n5/10 \u2014 Developer-facing quality-of-life improvement. Reduces manual triage time when hooks fail or MCP becomes stale. Valuable but not blocking any other active work. Issue #950 (SubagentStop task-completion failures) motivated this item; that hook path is already documented and the residue detection feature addresses a secondary maintenance concern.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Bottleneck: No single command exists to triage hook failures, MCP staleness, or stale state files \u2014 debugging requires reading 5 separate locations manually.\\n- Blocks: Nothing currently blocked by absence of this command.\\n- Benefits: Developers experiencing hook non-firing or MCP stale-data issues can run one command and get a structured remediation report instead of a manual 5-step checklist.\\n- Unblocks: Easier onboarding for new contributors unfamiliar with the plugin's internal wiring.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Single-command triage replaces a 5-step manual checklist documented in the item description.\\n- Structured `OK|WARN|FAIL` output with remediation hints makes errors actionable without reading source files.\\n- `--residue` mode catches dangling markdown links and removed-skill references before they propagate into user-visible failures.\\n- Exit codes (0/1/2) make the script CI-friendly \u2014 can be added to a pre-commit or pre-push gate.\\n- Follows the PEP 723 inline script pattern already established by 16 other scripts in the same directory, so no new tooling or dependency management is required.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nRunning `uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/dh_doctor.py` produces a structured five-line report:\\n\\n```\\n[OK]   Hook wiring: 7/7 hooks reference existing scripts\\n[OK]   MCP servers: backlog (responded 0.4s), sam (responded 0.3s)\\n[OK]   State dir: ~/.dh/projects/-home-user-claude_skills/ (12 plan files, 3 backlog files)\\n[OK]   Plugin cache: source 7.11.54 == cache 7.11.54\\n[OK]   No residue detected\\nExit: 0\\n```\\n\\nWhen a check fails, that line shows `[FAIL]` with a concrete remediation hint. When a check yields a warning (e.g., orphaned active-task file older than 24h), it shows `[WARN]`. Exit code is 0 (all OK), 1 (any FAIL), or 2 (any WARN with no FAIL).\\n\\nWith `--residue` flag: additionally checks every markdown link in `plugins/development-harness/skills/**/*.md` and `agents/*.md` resolves to an existing file, and every skill name referenced in agent prompts matches an existing skill directory. A broken link produces `[FAIL]` naming the file and the broken reference.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA new file `plugins/development-harness/scripts/dh_doctor.py` using PEP 723 inline script metadata (the pattern used by all 16 existing scripts in that directory). The script is invoked as a standalone command via `uv run --script` \u2014 no integration with existing scripts required. It performs the five checks in sequence, collects per-check results, and emits a report to stdout. Exit code is computed from the highest severity result across all checks.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/dh_doctor.py` exits 0 and prints one `[OK]` line per check when the plugin is correctly wired.\\n2. Each hook entry in `hooks.json` is verified: the referenced script path exists and the file is non-empty. A missing or empty script produces `[FAIL]`.\\n3. MCP reachability check calls at least one backlog MCP tool (`backlog_view` or `backlog_list`) and one SAM MCP tool (`sam_list`) and reports response time. A timeout or error produces `[FAIL]`.\\n4. State directory check confirms `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/` exists with `plan/`, `backlog/`, and `context/` subdirectories. An active-task file older than 24h produces `[WARN]`.\\n5. Plugin cache check compares `version` field in source `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` against version in `~/.claude/plugins/cache/*/development-harness/*/plugin.json`. A mismatch produces `[WARN]` with both version strings.\\n6. With `--residue` flag: every markdown link (`[text](./path)`) in `plugins/development-harness/skills/**/*.md` and `plugins/development-harness/agents/*.md` is checked for existence. A non-existent target produces `[FAIL]` naming the source file and the broken link target.\\n7. Exit code is 0 when all checks are `[OK]`, 1 when any check is `[FAIL]`, 2 when any check is `[WARN]` and none is `[FAIL]`.\\n8. The script uses PEP 723 inline metadata (`# /// script` block) \u2014 `uv run --script` requires no separate installation step.\\n9. All remediation hints in `[FAIL]` and `[WARN]` lines are concrete (a file path, a command to run, or a version string) \u2014 not generic advice.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 the 7-hook manifest this script verifies |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-context-direct-writes.cjs` \u2014 example hook script (Node.js) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/scripts/dh_migrate.py` \u2014 example PEP 723 inline script in same directory |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` \u2014 MCP server script; reachability check calls tools it exposes |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 source version field for cache freshness check |\\n| Research | `research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md` \u2014 `harness doctor` and `harness doctor --residue` patterns from external harness project |\\n| Research | `research/insights/2026-05-07-claude-code-harness-improvements.md` \u2014 improvement proposal context (item #2184 entry) |\\n| Skill | `/dh:backlog` \u2014 MCP tool reference for reachability check implementation |\\n| Agent | `@dh:backlog-item-groomer` \u2014 n/a (not applicable to implementation) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 standalone script, no dependency on other open backlog items.\\n- Blocks: None identified.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the script performs file-existence checks, JSON parsing, subprocess calls to MCP tools, and string pattern matching against markdown. All techniques are present in existing scripts in the same directory. Estimated 2-4 hours including the `--residue` markdown-link checker. The markdown link parser should use `marko` (per CLAUDE.md) rather than regex.\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new script `plugins/development-harness/scripts/dh_doctor.py` exposed via `uv run --script`. It performs five checks and emits a structured report:\\n\\n1. **Hook wiring** \u2014 every entry in `hooks/hooks.json` references a script that exists, is executable (or invocable via `node`/`uv run`), and the matcher pattern is valid\\n2. **MCP server reachability** \u2014 `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view` and `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan` both respond within 30s\\n3. **State directory hygiene** \u2014 `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/` exists, has expected subdirs (`plan/`, `backlog/`, `context/`), no orphaned active-task files older than 24h\\n4. **Plugin cache freshness** \u2014 version in `~/.claude/plugins/cache/.../plugin.json` matches version in source `plugin.json`\\n5. **Residue detection (`--residue` flag)** \u2014 every markdown link in `plugins/development-harness/skills/**/*.md` and `agents/*.md` resolves to an existing file; every skill name referenced in agent prompts matches an existing skill directory\\n\\nEach check returns `OK | WARN | FAIL` with a concrete remediation hint. Exit code is 0 when all OK, 1 when any FAIL, 2 when any WARN with no FAIL.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/dh_doctor.py`\\n\\nExpected output:\\n\\n```\\n[OK]   Hook wiring: 7/7 hooks reference existing scripts\\n[OK]   MCP servers: backlog (responded 0.4s), sam (responded 0.3s)\\n[OK]   State dir: ~/.dh/projects/-home-user-claude_skills/ (12 plan files, 3 backlog files)\\n[OK]   Plugin cache: source 7.11.54 == cache 7.11.54\\n[OK]   No residue detected\\nExit: 0\\n```\\n\\nRun with `--residue` flag and a deliberately broken markdown link: exit 1, output names the broken link.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe development-harness plugin has no equivalent diagnostic command. When hooks fail to fire, when MCP server tools return stale data, when SubagentStop hook does not mark tasks complete (issue #950), the user has no single command to run to triage. The current debugging path is manual:\\n\\n1. Read `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` to verify the hook is registered\\n2. Read each hook script to check it exists and has the right shebang\\n3. Run `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view` to verify MCP server reachability\\n4. Check `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/` for stale state files\\n5. Compare plugin cache version against `plugin.json` version\\n\\nThere is no `harness doctor` script that walks this checklist. There is also no `--residue` mode that detects leftover references to deleted skills, agents, or hooks from previous plugin versions (e.g., a SKILL.md referencing a now-deleted reference file, an agent prompt mentioning a removed skill).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"595d307b73bc1d2dcec5077243fe959e4a8a68c3ed8bf32cdd1f39837d57b7bd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPtX9cQ\"}"}